{
  "short_id": "short259",
  "episode_id": "PD-2026-062-greene",
  "voice_stage": "draft",
  "voice_id": "nPczCjzI2devNBz1zQrb",
  "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2",
  "estimated_cost_usd": 0.306,
  "total_seconds": 56.62,
  "master": "H:\\pd-media\\episodes\\PD-2026-062-greene\\06_voice\\draft\\short259\\en_us\\short259_vc_draft_en_us_v002.mp3",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "L1",
      "chunk_id": "L1",
      "delivery": "intense",
      "text": "The men who taped eviction notices to doors were asked under oath whether children pulled them down. One answered: they had plenty of trouble.",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.92,
      "seconds": 6.92,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:8ceb373b3e80f1e86dde27aa7024959b2549c842deb25d08bb9157d1f123c550"
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "chunk_id": "L2",
      "delivery": "building",
      "text": "He said he had seen children do it at Village West. That testimony was about the servers' experience, not proof about these three tenants' doors.",
      "start": 7.14,
      "end": 15.453,
      "seconds": 8.313,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:eeeeb266aa28a66f837dcb18c1229b55444d6bc5d84bca785f78eacbfa1dd733"
    },
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "chunk_id": "L3",
      "delivery": "building",
      "text": "The three tenants said they never saw the summonses and learned of the cases only after default judgments and writs of possession.",
      "start": 15.673,
      "end": 22.221,
      "seconds": 6.548,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:81a4046b0b3842ff02c8c8912ded459844d918e16055c13415e1b478c6b97119"
    },
    {
      "id": "L4",
      "chunk_id": "L4",
      "delivery": "building",
      "text": "The Court said posted notices were removed often enough that the papers failed before they could do the job notice was supposed to do.",
      "start": 22.441,
      "end": 29.221,
      "seconds": 6.78,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:98c850b25cf5d13fa2e297f0c62eda5a71d574407b47a9b6eeed5f849935f0d9"
    },
    {
      "id": "L5",
      "chunk_id": "L5",
      "delivery": "building",
      "text": "It did not say paper on a door always fails. In many situations, the Court said, posting can be appropriate and effective.",
      "start": 29.441,
      "end": 36.964,
      "seconds": 7.523,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:7a813a258f7b4803ddb76a5d67f0965f40a36cf0c29b81e6cc00cec18bfa404d"
    },
    {
      "id": "L6",
      "chunk_id": "L6",
      "delivery": "building",
      "text": "But on this record, merely posting on an apartment door did not meet the minimum standards of due process.",
      "start": 37.184,
      "end": 43.268,
      "seconds": 6.084,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:a1416a9c8e4ab9e10c38d10a4fce121246bb76c5783a2c36f9370414d58d14ef"
    },
    {
      "id": "L7",
      "chunk_id": "L7",
      "delivery": "building",
      "text": "The tenants had already lost by default and lost their chance to appeal before, they said, they knew proceedings existed.",
      "start": 43.488,
      "end": 50.175,
      "seconds": 6.687,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:6bc8fdca126d29b61308b740368a7688951094cb5b50ec7e4925285393f46620"
    },
    {
      "id": "L8",
      "chunk_id": "L8",
      "delivery": "calm",
      "text": "The ruling began with what the men posting the papers already knew: sometimes the notice did not stay where they put it.",
      "start": 50.395,
      "end": 56.618,
      "seconds": 6.223,
      "idempotency_key": "sha256:5b473759e848c7c5a8ae0fe101368116b7c834a7bcd099830e02f5dbc09814b1"
    }
  ]
}
